From 986a6cb038e205590255255703f94e008a720fe1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael <michael@lingxia.app>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:59:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] feat: resolve sizing keywords on min and max sizes

`min-width: min-content`, `max-height: fit-content` and the other sizing keywords are valid
on the min/max size properties, but the style type was `LengthPercentageAuto`, so they could
not be expressed. `min_size`/`max_size` are now `Size<Dimension>`. Flexbox, block and
absolutely positioned layout measure the item under the keyword's constraint: a flex item's
main axis when its flex base size is determined and its cross axis before its hypothetical
cross size (stretched items included), a block item's width and, when definite, its height,
and an absolutely positioned box against its containing block. Grid treats a keyword minimum
as `auto` and a keyword maximum as `none`.
